   → build_structure_phylo_tree
     Build a structure-based phylogenetic tree across simulations.
     
     CA coordinates are extracted from each simulation's PDB structure. For each
     pair, the sequence-aligned common residues are superposed (Kabsch) and the
     resulting CA-RMSD becomes the structural distance. The distance matrix is
     clustered (UPGMA) and rendered as an unrooted phylogram.
     
     Args:
         sim_dirs (required): Per-simulation working directories (parallel to ``labels``).
         labels (required): Simulation labels (e.g. UniProt-style ids).
         working_dir (required): Combined analysis output directory (base/analysis).
         base_dir (optional): Base multi-sim directory that holds ``{label}.pdb`` inputs.
         label_name_map (optional): Optional {label: protein_name} for display labels.
         user_goal (optional): Goal text (used to parse a name map if none is supplied).
     
     Returns:
         Dict with ``success``, ``plot_path`` (structure_phylo_tree.png),
         ``newick_file``, ``distance_matrix_csv``, ``n_structures``, ``labels``.

   → plot_dccm_comparison
     Create a side-by-side comparison heatmap of DCCM matrices from multiple
     simulations for combined / multi-simulation reports.
     
     Reads the per-simulation DCCM CSV files produced by ``calculate_dccm``
     (columns: residue_i, residue_j, correlation) and renders them as a
     single multi-panel figure.  Residue axes are aligned across panels.
     
     A difference panel (last simulation minus first) is appended when exactly
     two simulations are compared **and** they share identical residue numbering
     (e.g. apo vs holo of the same protein). For cross-protein comparisons
     (JAK1 vs TYK2), each panel shows the full matrix and no Δ panel is drawn
     because residue indices are not structurally equivalent.
     
     Args:
         dccm_files (required): Ordered list of DCCM CSV file paths (one per simulation).
             Each file must have columns ``residue_i, residue_j, correlation``.
         labels (required): Human-readable labels (one per file, same order).
         output_file (required): Output image filename (e.g. ``"dccm_comparison.png"``).
             Saved inside *working_dir*.
         working_dir (required): Directory where the figure is written.
         vmin (optional): Common colour scale minimum (default: −1.0).
         vmax (optional): Common colour scale maximum (default: +1.0).
         figsize_per_panel (optional): Width (and height) in inches for each panel
             (default: 5.0).
         dpi (optional): Image resolution (default: 200).
         cmap (optional): Matplotlib diverging colormap (default: ``"RdBu_r"``).
     
             diff_vmin (optional): See tool defaults.
             diff_vmax (optional): See tool defaults.
             cmap_diff (optional): See tool defaults.
     Returns:
         Dict with ``success``, ``output_path``, ``n_panels``, ``message``.

   → plot_dccm_difference
     Compute and plot the difference between two DCCM matrices (ΔC = compare − reference).
     
     Typical use: quantify how ATP (or another ligand) changes protein correlated
     motions by comparing DCCM from ``protein only`` vs ``protein + ATP`` simulations.
     Run ``calculate_dccm`` on each trajectory first (same ``selection``, e.g.
     ``"protein and name CA"``), then pass the two CSV files here.
     
     Residue axes are aligned on the **intersection** of residue IDs in both CSVs,
     so protein-only and protein+ligand systems match by residue number.
     
     Args:
         reference_dccm_file (required): Baseline DCCM CSV (e.g. protein-only ``dccm.csv``).
         compare_dccm_file (required): Perturbed DCCM CSV (e.g. protein+ATP ``dccm.csv``).
         reference_label (optional): Label for baseline (plots / legend).
         compare_label (optional): Label for perturbed system.
         output_prefix (optional): Prefix for outputs: ``<prefix>.csv``, ``<prefix>_heatmap.png``,
             and (if ``plot_mode="with_matrices"``) ``<prefix>_panels.png``.
         working_dir (optional): Directory for output files.
         plot_mode (optional): ``"difference_only"`` (default) — single Δ heatmap;
             ``"with_matrices"`` — reference, compare, and Δ in one figure.
         diff_threshold (optional): Report residue pairs with |ΔC| above this (default: 0.3).
         max_top_pairs (optional): Cap on reported pairs (default: 50).
         dpi (optional): PNG resolution.
     
             vmin_corr (optional): See tool defaults.
             vmax_corr (optional): See tool defaults.
             diff_vmin (optional): See tool defaults.
             diff_vmax (optional): See tool defaults.
             cmap_corr (optional): See tool defaults.
             cmap_diff (optional): See tool defaults.
     Returns:
         Dict with ``success``, ``delta_matrix_stats``, ``top_changed_pairs``,
         ``output_files``, ``n_residues_aligned``, ``message``.

